        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William McKendree Gwin, John Charles Frémont\n- Roles: medical doctor, politician, explorer, soldier, presidential candidate\n- Places: Mississippi, California, United States\n- Organizations: Republican Party\n- Events: 1856 United States presidential candidacy\n\nFacts:\n- William McKendree Gwin was born on October 9, 1805.\n- William McKendree Gwin was an American medical doctor and politician.\n- William McKendree Gwin served in elected office in Mississippi and California.\n- In California, William McKendree Gwin shared a distinction with John Charles Frémont.\n- John Charles Frémont was an American explorer, politician, and soldier.\n- In 1856, John Charles Frémont became the first candidate of the anti-war Republican Party for President of the United States.\n- William McKendree Gwin died on September 3, 1885.",
